      "text": "Tropical rainforests home more than half of the world's species in just a small fraction of its land area. Every tree cut down represents the potential loss of organisms we haven't even gotten to know. Deforestation advances mainly through agricultural and livestock expansion. Restoring these ecosystems takes decades, while destroying them takes just a few days.",
